    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties. Everything turns on one charge line: the SGD 3.20 ERP line for the gantry 'Bukit Merah Central westbound', charged at 2026-09-21T11:43:00 on trip TRP-09114. Rider — you are refunded the full SGD 3.20 you contested, which is the whole of the contested amount. Your ride was an upfront-quoted fare: the booking quoted SGD 22.00 and the ledger's total_charged is SGD 25.20. The entire SGD 3.20 difference is that single ERP line — airport_surcharge and waiting_time_fee are both 0.00, and the base, distance, time and platform-fee lines all sit inside the SGD 22.00 quote. The GPS trace for this trip is complete and unimpaired: 169 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, coverage_pct 100.0, gaps empty, max_gap_sec 0.0, running 11:30:00 to 11:58:00. Against that trace the gantry's coordinates (lat 1.34, lng 103.78) lie 7,482.07 m from the nearest fix, index 65 at 11:40:50 — nowhere near the 250 m radius POL-RD-09 uses to treat a fix as a crossing. The vehicle never passed the gantry, so under POL-RD-09(4) the line is a billing-integrity failure and is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not any deviation exists; that limb expressly does not trigger POL-RD-10(8) where it is the only unmatched line. POL-RD-11(a) reaches the same SGD 3.20 independently: on an upfront quote only pass-throughs actually incurred (ERP and tolls crossed, a properly chargeable airport surcharge, waiting_time_fee) may sit on top of the quoted fare, and this one was not incurred. The final amount payable is rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 and SGD 3.20 is unchanged. Driver — nothing is found against you on the money and nothing is taken from you. The trace records 16.0 km against the 12.5 km optimal route, an excess of 3.5 km (28.00%), which clears POL-RD-01's two establishment tests (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) but is below both materiality thresholds (50% and 8.0 km absolute), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no driver-conduct referral issues; in any event your profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern exists. POL-RD-11 means the distance and time charges on an upfront-quoted trip are fixed at booking, so no fare recomputation runs against you, and your unrecovered cost on an unjustified detour is not recoverable from the rider under that clause. Your own statement that the route 'was longer than expected' but that you 'did not see or pass the gantry named on the receipt' corroborates the trace; note that a counterparty statement carries no weight_multiplier, so it supports the finding but does not enter the confidence cap. Confidence is 0.95, within the cap of 1.0: the deciding fact — that the gantry was never crossed — is carried by two independent artifacts at weight 1.0, the GPS trace EV-GPS-09114 and the fare breakdown EV-FARE-09114. Claims considered: both sides agree POL-RD-11 governs and that the only recoverable item on this fare is the SGD 3.20 ERP line — accepted, and it is the outcome. The rider's POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity claim — accepted, producing both the refund and the referral above. The rider's POL-RD-01 deviation finding of 3.5 km / 28.00% — accepted, but on an upfront quote it moves no money. The POL-RD-06 materiality and repeat-pattern points from both sides — accepted; no material deviation, no pattern, no conduct referral. The rider's POL-RD-07 trace-integrity claim — accepted; the trace is unimpaired, so no corroboration or down-weighting rule is engaged. The rider's POL-RD-04 chat-log claim — accepted; the log holds one rider message at 11:53:00 with waypoint_hint null, naming no road or place and sent after the 11:43:00 charge, so it is no detour instruction and POL-RD-09(3) does not defeat the ERP refund. The rider's POL-RD-03 point that no advisory exists — accepted; the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-09114-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, so no closure or advisory can exonerate anything. A POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral is recorded in the rulings list; it rides with the money and does not displace it. Open question for the reviewer, which belongs here rather than in the referrals list: why a gantry 7.5 km off the driven corridor was billed at all — the record shows no system cause, and the reviewer may wish to trace the ERP billing source.",
    "referrals_note": null
  },
